# Contributing Guidelines

When contributing to the @10up/block-components project, follow these guidelines:

## Code Contribution Process

- Fork the repository
- Create a feature branch from the `develop` branch
- Follow the coding standards and guidelines
- Submit a pull request back to the `develop` branch
- Ensure all tests pass
- Include appropriate documentation

## Component Contributions

- All new components should have a clear, focused purpose
- Components should be reusable and configurable
- Include appropriate PropTypes or TypeScript interfaces
- Document the component's usage in a readme.md file
- Export the component from the appropriate index.ts file
- Consider adding tests for the component

## Documentation

- Include JSDoc comments for all functions, methods, and components
- Document props, parameters, and return values
- Update existing documentation when changing functionality
- Provide usage examples in component readme files

## Testing

- Add tests for new functionality
- Update tests when changing existing code
- Ensure backwards compatibility when possible
- Test in both editor and frontend contexts when applicable

## Versioning

- Follow semantic versioning
- Breaking changes should be clearly documented
- Deprecate features before removing them when possible

